course: dictionary
lesson: 7122
title: One word, many meanings: peg
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peg is a small thing that holds something else. Read the words around the word to find out which kind of peg it is. «The Mole's cap was missing from its accustomed peg.» A cap is worn on your head, and it hangs on a peg on the wall, so a peg here is a hook.
explain: «Grandad Ray in Leeds pegs a washing line across the garden.» Pegs is used as a verb here, a doing word. He is fastening the washing to the line, so to peg means to fasten something with pegs.
explain: «Leave a campsite as you found it, and walk carefully between tents because ropes and pegs trip people up.» Tent pegs are pointed sticks pushed into the ground. The clue is the tent and the ropes, which the pegs hold in place.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: A peg can be a small hook or stick on a wall for hanging things, like coats and bags.
fact: A clothes peg is a small clip for hanging washing on a line.
fact: A tent peg is a pointed stick pushed into the ground to hold a tent.
fact: «Take someone down a peg» means to make a proud person less proud.
fact: Peg can also be a verb: to peg something is to fasten it with pegs.
exercise: «The Mole's cap was missing from its accustomed peg.» Where did the cap usually hang? | *A peg on the wall | A table | The floor under the bed | The bottom of the river
exercise: «Grandad Ray in Leeds pegs a washing line across the garden.» What is Grandad doing? | Cooking dinner for the family | Digging a hole for a tree | *Fastening washing to the line with clips | Painting the fence
exercise: Why do campers hammer tent pegs into the ground? | To wash the plates | To cook their dinner | To make a path for the walk | *To hold the tent down
test: «Walk carefully between tents because ropes and pegs trip people up.» What should people do at a campsite? | Shout loudly to their friends | *Walk carefully between the tents | Run fast between the tents | Sit down in the middle of the ropes
test: If you take someone down a peg, what do you do? | *Make a proud person less proud | Make them taller | Give them a prize | Hang them on a hook
exam: Which of these is a clothes peg? | A bag on a school shelf | *A small clip for hanging washing on a line | A hook for a coat on the wall | A pointed stick pushed into the ground
